# riscv_terminal in the emulator's window (ECP5_GUI_SCRIPT; see gui/src/trace.rs).
# The window runs it at about 0.2-0.9 MHz and opens the Monitor window by
# itself when the design drives the GPDI pads: the shell's output appears on
# the monitor as it is typed into the UART console. Typed text waits in the
# design's 511-byte FIFO, so commands can be sent while the shell is busy.
# The Mandelbrot picture is the long pole: about 20 s at 0.2 MHz. The button
# is held for two seconds: the design debounces it for 10 ms (250 000 clocks), and the window runs about 0.25 MHz.
0 rate max
0 run
1 board 3d
2 type help\r
12 type led 5a\r
17 type mandel\r
55 type screen\r
74 button 1 down   # FIRE1: an event line, on the UART and on the monitor
76 button 1 up
90 quit
